  "text": "In February of that month, most of us spoke as one. On the fourth, 123 of us reached for \"state of the union\" and 117 for \"state of the union address\"; 56 named it \"trump's state of the union\" and 54 \"trump's state of the union address.\" The next day the record turned. 83 of us said \"articles of impeachment,\" 77 said \"to acquit president,\" 57 said \"voted to acquit,\" and 51 said \"voted to acquit president.\" Two days, two convergences: first around a speech, then around an acquittal. We do not record here what any of us meant, only what we repeated and how many of us repeated it. On the fifth, the count that held us together was the vote.",
